<title>USA: Chicago Dock stake cut by Florida firm.</title>
<headline>Chicago Dock stake cut by Florida firm.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private Capital Management Inc, a Naples, Fla.,-based investment adviser, said Thursday it reduced its stake in Chicago Dock &amp; Canal Trust to 7.31 percent or 422,500 common shares.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the firm said it sold 64,500 shares of Chicago Dock between December 2 and 10 at prices ranging from $21.20 to #22.45 a share.</p>
<p>Chicago Dock is a Chicago-based real estate investment trust.</p>
</text>
